"""Level 5 exam content: Week 8 midterm (Lessons 1-7) and Week 15 final (all 13 lessons, most items from Lessons 8-13).
Every word and grammar point comes from the Level 5 lessons (level5/curriculum/Level5_Lesson*.md) and the Level 5 Scope and Sequence §7.
make_exam_md.py turns this into the student tests, the teacher packets and the listening scripts; check_consistency.py checks them.
Listening/reading item: q (stem), kind ('mc' circle a/b/c | 'tf' true/false | 'write' one word), opts, ans, les (lesson),
ev (the words in the audio or text that give the answer), keys (answer words that must be in ev; default: the answer),
heard (wrong options that ARE in the audio or text on purpose).
An exam may override level settings in cfg (Level 5: a paragraph at the midterm, a letter at the final)."""
LEVEL = 5

def it(q, kind, ans, les, ev, opts=(), keys=None, heard=()):
    return dict(q=q, kind=kind, opts=list(opts), ans=ans, les=les, ev=ev, keys=keys, heard=list(heard))

